          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Async-Signal-Safety",
          "text": "malloc and printf take locks the interrupted code may already hold — calling them in a handler can deadlock. Set a flag or write one byte to a self-pipe or eventfd, then do the real work in the main loop."
